  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rural Electrification Project through Renewal Energy under Reverse Linkage</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed project aims to support Niger in addressing the critical issues of lack of electricity in rural areas by contributing to increase the electricity access rate. The project will increase the power generation through the establishment of three solar power plants with a total capacity of 9.3 MWp that will be distributed using the network composed of about 144 km of MV lines, 112 km of LV lines, and distribution transformers of 8 MVA for about 17,500 consumers&#x2019; connections using prepaid meters. By the completion of the project, about 17,500 households for a targeted population of 122,500 (comprising about 51% of women), 1,500 public facilities (schools, health centers, etc.) as well as small businesses will be connected.</narrative>
  </description>
